Article 22
Efforts to increase the role, quality and capability of women in the field include:
a. implementing programs, activities, training for improving the skills and expertise of women in order to realize the improvement of women's welfare;
b. facilitation of business capital strengthening for women who have weak economies;
c. marketing of products resulting from the businesses of women who have weak economies;
d. training for developing women's capabilities through economic empowerment of pre-prosperous families;
e. entrepreneurship training for women comprehensively.

Article 21
Efforts to enhance the role, quality and capability of women in the social field include:
a. enhancement of knowledge and skills to encourage the fulfillment of education in accordance with the potential possessed;
b. enhancement and fulfillment of health quality for women;
c. enhancement of awareness and knowledge about independent, healthy and prosperous family planning including access to consultation services and marriage registration;
d. enhancement of women's awareness of the impact of early marriage;
e. facilitating and endeavoring the preservation of customs and traditions and the development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women;
f. conducting enhancement of women's awareness and knowledge regarding independent, healthy and prosperous family planning;
g. conducting programs to reduce maternal mortality rates;
h. encouraging the establishment of women's organizations in the Region;

4.1.text:
Article 7
The obligations of Regional Government in efforts to protect women include:
a. establishing and implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women's rights;
b. conducting cooperation with the community and/or Community Organizations in the implementation of women's protection in accordance with laws and regulations;
c. conducting rehabilitation and empowerment of women who are victims of acts of violence;
d. providing special protection to women victims of acts of violence and human trafficking; and
e. taking preventive action in order to prevent violations of women's rights.

Article 25
The responsibility of parents and family to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children includes:
a. protecting women and children from various violations of rights in the household;
b. encouraging the formation of a harmonious, educational and democratic family;
c. providing good examples to children in accordance with religious and customary teachings;
d. supervising children in their activities inside or outside the home; and
e. providing opportunities for children to dialogue and express opinions democratically.

Article 23
(1) The responsibility of the Regional Government to prevent acts of violence against women and children includes:
a. conducting socialization regarding the prevention of violence against women and children by optimizing the role of customary, cultural, religious institutions and community organizations;
b. providing guidelines on handling acts of violence against women and children; c. involving community participation in recovery and reintegration;
d. developing an integrated database and information system on acts of violence against women and children;
e. developing family empowerment programs;
f. strengthening the function of community organizations engaged in women's empowerment and child protection; and
g. providing public facilities that are comfortable and safe for women and children.
(2) Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of: a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection; f. mental and spiritual;
g. informatics and communication; and h. public peace and order.
(3) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their respective fields of duty in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

Article 3
Women's Empowerment and Child Protection aims to: a. serve as a guideline for local government in planning, policies and strategies for the protection of women and children;
b. protect women and children from actions, decisions and policies that violate the rights of women and children; c. prevent violations of the rights of women and children;
d. increase empowerment of women and children;
e. enhance the role and value of local wisdom and the role of customs in the protection of women and children; and f. enhance the role of government and non-government institutions in the region in efforts to protect women and children.

Article 24
The responsibility of the community to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children includes:
a. monitoring various conditions that occur in their environment that may give rise to violations of the rights of women and children;
b. increasing awareness of violations of the rights of women and children;
c. strengthening the role of community organizations, religious organizations and the family environment; and
d. preventing unregistered marriages and marriage at child age.

